{%- doc -%}
  Renders the intro half of a product description: everything BEFORE the first
  "Dimensions:" heading.

  The Dimensions and Specifications blocks are already shown as rows in the
  Details & Dimensions tab, so repeating them in the Description tab is noise.
  The cut happens here, in Liquid, on the server - the trimmed copy is what is
  sent to the browser, so there is no flash of the old content and no layout
  shift. The description itself is never modified: the full text stays in the
  Shopify admin, which is what snippets/pdp-redo-description-label.liquid parses
  the Colour and Design rows out of.

  The heading is matched case-insensitively and works wherever it sits - bare
  text, <strong>, <b> or any <h1>-<h6> - because the search runs on a
  lower-cased copy of the raw HTML and cuts at the label itself, not at a tag.
  A description with no "Dimensions:" heading keeps all of its copy.

  Whatever is left at the end is then peeled off - after a cut or not - so the
  intro always ends on
  the last line of visible text: no empty paragraph, no half-open heading, and
  no blockquote or table shell left holding a border that would show up under
  the copy as a stray line. Images and other embedded media are kept.

  @param {object} product - the product object

  @example
    {% render 'pdp-redo-description-intro', product: product %}
{%- enddoc -%}
{%- liquid
  assign source = product.description
  assign intro = source

  if source != blank
    assign lower = source | downcase

    if lower contains 'dimensions:'
      comment
        downcase preserves length, so the offset measured on the lower-cased
        copy slices the original HTML at exactly the same point.
      endcomment
      assign cut = lower | split: 'dimensions:' | first | size
      assign intro = source | slice: 0, cut

      comment
        The cut can land inside a tag that was still being written out, leaving
        something like "<h3 class=" with no closing bracket. Peel that off first
        so the trailing markup below is always made of whole tags.
      endcomment
      for pass in (1..4)
        assign tail = intro | split: '<' | last
        unless tail contains '>'
          assign dangling = '<' | append: tail
          assign intro = intro | remove_last: dangling
        endunless
      endfor
    endif

    comment
      Now walk backwards from the end and drop everything that renders
      nothing. Two shapes turn up:

        - a tag that was opened and never filled - "<p>", "<span style=...>",
          "<br />" - which has nothing after it at all, so it goes;
        - an element that closes with no text in it - "<p></p>", an empty
          blockquote, a table shell - found by matching the closing tag back
          to the last opener of the same name and checking that what sits
          between them reads as blank.

      Judging by what an element renders rather than by a list of tag names is
      what keeps this working on markup nobody has seen yet: an empty
      blockquote or table cell still carries the theme's borders and appears
      under the copy as a stray line, and because each pass removes one
      element, nested shells unwind from the outside in on their own.

      Anything holding media is left alone - an intro is allowed to end on an
      image.
    endcomment
    assign media_tags = '<img,<iframe,<video,<audio,<source,<picture,<svg,<canvas,<object,<embed' | split: ','
    assign blank_tails = '&nbsp;,&#160;,&#xa0;,&#xA0;, ' | split: ','

    for pass in (1..40)
      assign intro = intro | strip

      comment
        Hard spaces survive strip, and a paragraph made of them is still an
        empty paragraph.
      endcomment
      for blank_tail in blank_tails
        assign blank_size = blank_tail | size
        assign blank_offset = 0 | minus: blank_size
        assign seen = intro | slice: blank_offset, blank_size
        if seen == blank_tail
          assign intro = intro | remove_last: blank_tail
          assign intro = intro | strip
        endif
      endfor

      if intro == blank
        break
      endif

      assign last_char = intro | slice: -1
      unless last_char == '>'
        break
      endunless

      assign inner = intro | split: '<' | last
      assign tag = '<' | append: inner
      assign name = inner | split: '>' | first | replace: '/', '' | split: ' ' | first | downcase
      assign is_closer = inner | slice: 0, 1

      unless is_closer == '/'
        comment
          An opening or void tag at the very end has nothing to show.
        endcomment
        assign intro = intro | remove_last: tag
        continue
      endunless

      comment
        Locate the opener this closer belongs to. Both spellings are
        measured - "<p>" and "<p " - and the later one wins, so a tag with
        attributes is found and "<p" never matches "<picture". The position
        is the length of the string minus everything that follows the last
        occurrence, which is how you get a last-index-of out of split.
      endcomment
      assign intro_size = intro | size
      assign open_plain = '<' | append: name | append: '>'
      assign open_attr = '<' | append: name | append: ' '
      assign open_at = -1

      assign chunks = intro | split: open_plain
      assign chunk_count = chunks | size
      if chunk_count > 1
        assign rest = chunks | last
        assign rest_size = rest | size
        assign open_size = open_plain | size
        assign open_at = intro_size | minus: rest_size | minus: open_size
      endif

      assign chunks = intro | split: open_attr
      assign chunk_count = chunks | size
      if chunk_count > 1
        assign rest = chunks | last
        assign rest_size = rest | size
        assign open_size = open_attr | size
        assign attr_at = intro_size | minus: rest_size | minus: open_size
        if attr_at > open_at
          assign open_at = attr_at
        endif
      endif

      if open_at < 0
        break
      endif

      assign element = intro | slice: open_at, intro_size

      assign holds_media = false
      for media_tag in media_tags
        if element contains media_tag
          assign holds_media = true
        endif
      endfor
      if holds_media
        break
      endif

      assign element_text = element | strip_html
      for blank_tail in blank_tails
        assign element_text = element_text | replace: blank_tail, ' '
      endfor
      assign element_text = element_text | strip

      if element_text == blank
        assign intro = intro | slice: 0, open_at
      else
        break
      endif
    endfor

    assign intro = intro | strip

    comment
      A description that runs the heading into the intro paragraph rather than
      giving it its own block leaves the paragraph open. Browsers close it
      themselves, but closing it here keeps the markup valid.
    endcomment
    comment
      The sentinel matters: split drops a trailing empty string, so counting
      closing tags on an intro that already ends in one comes back a tag
      short, and every intro would then gain a stray closer.
    endcomment
    assign counted = intro | append: '~END~'
    assign p_open = counted | split: '<p' | size | minus: 1
    assign p_close = counted | split: '</p>' | size | minus: 1
    if p_open > p_close
      assign intro = intro | append: '</p>'
    endif
  endif
-%}
{{ intro }}